:" Creates an array where each element is produced by calling `f` with"},{"DocComment":" that element's index while walking forward through the array."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" This is essentially the same as writing"},{"DocComment":" ```text"},{"DocComment":" [f(0), f(1), f(2), …, f(N - 2), f(N - 1)]"},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":" and is similar to `(0..i).map(f)`, just for arrays not iterators."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" If `N == 0`, this produces an empty array without ever calling `f`."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" # Example"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```rust"},{"DocComment":" // type inference is helping us here, the way `from_fn` knows how many"},{"DocComment":" // elements to produce is the length of array down there: only arrays of"},{"DocComment":" // equal lengths can be compared, so the const generic parameter `N` is"},{"DocComment":" // inferred to be 5, thus creating array of 5 elements."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" let array = core::array::from_fn(|i| i);"},{"DocComment":" // indexes are:    0  1  2  3  4"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(array, [0, 1, 2, 3, 4]);"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" let array2: [usize; 8] = core::array::from_fn(|i| i * 2);"},{"DocComment":" // indexes are:     0  1  2  3  4  5   6   7"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(array2, [0, 2, 4, 6, 8, 10, 12, 14]);"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" let bool_arr = core::array::from_fn::<_, 5, _>(|i| i % 2 == 0);"},{"DocComment":" // indexes are:       0     1      2     3      4"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(bool_arr, [true, false, true, false, true]);"},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" You can also capture things, for example to create an array full of clones"},{"DocComment":" where you can't just use `[item; N]` because it's not `Copy`:"},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":" let my_string: [String; 2] = std::array::from_fn(|i| format!(\"Hello {i}\"));"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(my_string, [\"Hello 0\", \"Hello 1\"]);"},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" The array is generated in ascending index order, starting from the front"},{"DocComment":" and going towards the back, so you can use closures with mutable state:"},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":" let mut state = 1;"},{"DocComment":" let a = std::array::from_fn(|_| { let x = state; state *= 2; x });"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(a, [1, 2, 4, 8, 16, 32]);"},{"DocComment":" ```"}],"inline":"Hint","rename":null,"public":true},"is_local":false,"opacity":"Foreign","lang_item":null},"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"index":0,"name":"T"},{"index":1,"name":"F"}],"const_generics":[{"index":0,"name":"N","ty":{"Deduplicated":981}}],"trait_clauses":[{"clause_id":0,"span":{"data":{"file_id":14,"beg":{"line":110,"col":24},"end":{"line":110,"col":40}},"generated_from_span":null},"origin":"WhereClauseOnFn","trait_":{"regions":[],"skip_binder":{"id":0,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"Deduplicated":11433}],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]}}}},{"clause_id":1,"span":{"data":{"file_id":14,"beg":{"line":112,"col":7},"end":{"line":112,"col":32}},"generated_from_span":null},"origin":"WhereClauseOnFn","trait_":{"regions":[],"skip_binder":{"id":1,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"Deduplicated":11436},{"Deduplicated":1560},{"Deduplicated":11433}],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]}}}},{"clause_id":2,"span":{"data":{"file_id":14,"beg":{"line":112,"col":35},"end":{"line":112,"col":51}},"generated_from_span":null},"origin":"WhereClauseOnFn","trait_":{"regions":[],"skip_binder":{"id":0,"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"Deduplicated":11436}],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]}}}}],"regions_outlive":[],"types_outlive":[],"trait_type_constraints":[]},"signature":{"is_unsafe":false,"abi":"Rust","is_variadic":false,"inputs":[{"Deduplicated":11436}],"output":{"HashConsedValue":[11448,{"Array":[{"Deduplicated":11433},{"kind":{"Var":{"Free":0}},"ty":{"Deduplicated":981}}]}]}},"src":"TopLevel","is_global_initializer":null,"body":"Opaque"},{"def_id":7,"item_meta":{"name":[{"Ident":["alloc",0]},{"Ident":["vec",0]},{"Impl":{"Ty":{"params":{"regions":[],"types":[{"index":0,"name":"T"}],"const_generics":[],"trait_clauses":[],"regions_outlive":[],"types_outlive":[],"trait_type_constraints":[]},"skip_binder":{"Deduplicated":10939},"kind":"InherentImplBlock"}}},{"Ident":["with_capacity",0]}],"span":{"data":{"file_id":4,"beg":{"line":523,"col":4},"end":{"line":523,"col":55}},"generated_from_span":null},"source_text":null,"attr_info":{"attributes":[{"DocComment":" Constructs a new, empty `Vec<T>` with at least the specified capacity."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" The vector will be able to hold at least `capacity` elements without"},{"DocComment":" reallocating. This method is allowed to allocate for more elements than"},{"DocComment":" `capacity`. If `capacity` is zero, the vector will not allocate."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" It is important to note that although the returned vector has the"},{"DocComment":" minimum *capacity* specified, the vector will have a zero *length*. For"},{"DocComment":" an explanation of the difference between length and capacity, see"},{"DocComment":" *[Capacity and reallocation]*."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" If it is important to know the exact allocated capacity of a `Vec`,"},{"DocComment":" always use the [`capacity`] method after construction."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" For `Vec<T>` where `T` is a zero-sized type, there will be no allocation"},{"DocComment":" and the capacity will always be `usize::MAX`."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" [Capacity and reallocation]: #capacity-and-reallocation"},{"DocComment":" [`capacity`]: Vec::capacity"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" # Panics"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Panics if the new capacity exceeds `isize::MAX` _bytes_."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" # Examples"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":" let mut vec = Vec::with_capacity(10);"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" // The vector contains no items, even though it has capacity for more"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(vec.len(), 0);"},{"DocComment":" assert!(vec.capacity() >= 10);"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" // These are all done without reallocating..."},{"DocComment":" for i in 0..10 {"},{"DocComment":"     vec.push(i);"},{"DocComment":" }"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(vec.len(), 10);"},{"DocComment":" assert!(vec.capacity() >= 10);"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" // ...but this may make the vector reallocate"},{"DocComment":" vec.push(11);"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(vec.len(), 11);"},{"DocComment":" assert!(vec.capacity() >= 11);"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" // A vector of a zero-sized type will always over-allocate, since no"},{"DocComment":" // allocation is necessary"},{"DocComment":" let vec_units = Vec::<()>::with_capacity(10);"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(vec_units.capacity(), usize::MAX);"},{"DocComment":" ```"}],"inline":"Hint","rename":null,"public":true},"is_local":false,"opacity":"Foreign","lang_item":"vec_with_capacity"},"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"index":0,"name":"T"}],"const_generics":[],"trait_clauses":[],"regions_outlive":[],"types_outlive":[],"trait_type_constraints":[]},"signature":{"is_unsafe":false,"abi":"Rust","is_variadic":false,"inputs":[{"Deduplicated":981}],"output":{"HashConsedValue":[11439,{"Adt":{"id":{"Adt":2},"generics":{"regions":[],"types":[{"Deduplicated":11433}],"const_generics":[],"trait_refs":[]}}}]}},"src":"TopLevel","is_global_initializer":null,"body":"Opaque"},{"def_id":8,"item_meta":{"name":[{"Ident":["core",0]},{"Ident":["slice",0]},{"Impl":{"Ty":{"params":{"regions":[],"types":[{"index":0,"name":"T"}],"const_generics":[],"trait_clauses":[],"regions_outlive":[],"types_outlive":[],"trait_type_constraints":[]},"skip_binder":{"Deduplicated":1421},"kind":"InherentImplBlock"}}},{"Ident":["chunks_exact",0]}],"span":{"data":{"file_id":13,"beg":{"line":1243,"col":4},"end":{"line":1243,"col":77}},"generated_from_span":null},"source_text":null,"attr_info":{"attributes":[{"DocComment":" Returns an iterator over `chunk_size` elements of the slice at a time, starting at the"},{"DocComment":" beginning of the slice."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" The chunks are slices and do not overlap. If `chunk_size` does not divide the length of the"},{"DocComment":" slice, then the last up to `chunk_size-1` elements will be omitted and can be retrieved"},{"DocComment":" from the `remainder` function of the iterator."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Due to each chunk having exactly `chunk_size` elements, the compiler can often optimize the"},{"DocComment":" resulting code better than in the case of [`chunks`]."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" See [`chunks`] for a variant of this iterator that also returns the remainder as a smaller"},{"DocComment":" chunk, and [`rchunks_exact`] for the same iterator but starting at the end of the slice."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" If your `chunk_size` is a constant, consider using [`as_chunks`] instead, which will"},{"DocComment":" give references to arrays of exactly that length, rather than slices."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" # Panics"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" Panics if `chunk_size` is zero."},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" # Examples"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":" let slice = ['l', 'o', 'r', 'e', 'm'];"},{"DocComment":" let mut iter = slice.chunks_exact(2);"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(iter.next().unwrap(), &['l', 'o']);"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(iter.next().unwrap(), &['r', 'e']);"},{"DocComment":" assert!(iter.next().is_none());"},{"DocComment":" assert_eq!(iter.remainder(), &['m']);"},{"DocComment":" ```"},{"DocComment":""},{"DocComment":" [`chunks`]: slice::chunks"},{"DocComment":" [`rchunks_exact`]: slice::rchunks_exact"},{"DocComment":" [`as_chunks`]: slice::as_chunks"}],"inline":"Hint","rename":null,"public":true},"is_local":false,"opacity":"Foreign","lang_item":null}